So, in code terms, it would be something like: for pos in 1 to 9:
    for prev_d in 0 to 9:
        for mod in 0 to 10:
            if DP[pos][prev_d][mod] > 0:
                for d in 0 to prev_d:
                    if pos+1 is odd:
                        new_mod = (mod + d) % 11
                    else:
                        new_mod = (mod - d) % 11
                    DP[pos+1][d][new_mod] += DP[pos][prev_d][mod]

Thus, the number of 10-digit numbers which are multiples of 11 and have non-increasing digits is: \[
\boxed{3978}
\]
